r=A.b([new A.f4("\ud83c\udf0d","1 \xb7 Supported environments",i),new A.f4("\ud83d\udef0\ufe0f","2 \xb7 Production support (what is online)",h),new A.f4("\ud83d\udd00","3 \xb7 How to switch Development \u2194 Production",g),new A.f4(f,"4 \xb7 Current active environment (LIVE)",A.b(["Active profile: "+e,"Mode: "+d.b+"  ("+c+")","Anchor URL in use: "+b,"API base in use: "+a,"Connection: "+s],j)),new A.f4("\ud83d\udda5\ufe0f","5 \xb7 The phases at a glance + Phase 2 shell (LOCAL \xb7 DEVELOPMENT)",A.b(["Phase 1 = the original local proof (single machine, app talks to the local backend directly). Phase 2 = the same, PLUS the anchor running locally so web/mobile go through it (mimics production). Phase 3 = anchor + web ONLINE.","Config per phase: Phase 2 uses DEVELOPMENT config (local); Phase 3 uses PRODUCTION config (online domain). Phase 2 is unchanged and always stays on development.",'Command: ./phase2_up.sh  \u2014 asks "with the anchor?" and brings up locally: brain :8000, anchor :9100, request page :9104/anchor_sim.html, webhook :9300, Flutter web :8080, desktop, iOS simulator.',"Use this to test the whole flow end-to-end on your Mac before anything goes online."],j)),new A.f4("\u2601\ufe0f","6 \xb7 What the Phase 3 shell provides (ONLINE / PRODUCTION)",A.b(["Command: ./phase3_up.sh  \u2014 a standalone script (works without the loop/agent).","DEPLOYS FROM COPIES: keeps deploy_anchor/ + deploy_web/ copies of the successful folders and deploys by OVERWRITING the VM folders from those copies. Your original folders are never edited.","CHANGE-DETECTION: compares originals vs copies. First run deploys even with no diff; later runs SKIP when nothing changed, and ASK you before deploying when a change is found.","LEVERAGES existing infra \u2014 never recreates the reverse proxy, the SSL (valid Let's Encrypt, never self-signed), the domain, or the Postgres DB (created only if missing, never recreated).","Postgres: the anchor runs on Postgres via its own isolated venv; connectivity is verified through the REAL app path (a submitted request lands as a row in the DB).","Auto-selects Production and opens ONLY the main players: request page, online anchor, online web, desktop, mobile simulator. Brain + poller run in the background (no windows)."],j)),new A.f4("\ud83d\udd01","6b \xb7 The loop (anchor_loop.sh) + resilience",A.b(["anchor_loop.sh is the control loop: you type phase2 / phase3 / stop / done, and it also gives the agent (Claude / Cowork) a CLI bridge to drive + analyze runs with you, on your Mac terminal.","The SAME tools work locally in Phase 2 with the local env (localhost) \u2014 identical behavior, just different URLs.","This guide is synchronized across desktop, mobile, and web \u2014 you see the same helper everywhere."],j)),new A.f4("\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f","6c \xb7 Lessons baked into phase3 (won't recur)",A.b(["WHOLE-FOLDER overwrite from the copy, so every anchor dependency ships (no missing-module crash).","The anchor's isolated venv (with psycopg2) is PRESERVED across deploys; the service runs on the venv python.","The web is built with --base-href /odin-web/ so its assets load under the subpath (no stuck loading).","Each privileged step is its own SSH call so sudo authenticates; reset-failed clears any start-limit before start.",'DB verified through the app (request \u2192 row), never just "service exists". Valid SSL/domain/proxy reused; other Azure sites untouched.'],j)),new A.f4("\ud83e\uddea","7 \xb7 How to use Phase 3 for testing",A.b(['After I confirm readiness, type "phase3" in the loop. The shell opens everything for you.',"Your only job: send a message from the app/simulator \u2192 confirm the 3rd-party page receives it \u2192 send a reply from the 3rd party \u2192 confirm the simulator receives it, all over the REAL IP.","Watch the CD-flow on :9104 (Production) and the per-project webhook response blocks.","If a request seems slow, that is expected \u2014 production is asynchronous (queued through the anchor)."],j)),new A.f4("\ud83d\udcf1","8 \xb7 Simulator vs real-device testing",A.b(["Simulator FIRST: I can read the live mobile logs while it runs, so we fix any issue against real logs before your phone.","On the simulator you should see: the Odin icon + name, the login screen, then (after first login) the Face ID unlock on return.","When set to Production, the app talks to https://anchor.odinmarkets.com/odin-anchor \u2014 confirm the top-bar shows PRODUCTION so you never test against the wrong environment.","Real phone comes AFTER the simulator passes \u2014 then I depend on your description (no direct logs), so we lock it down on the simulator first."],j)),new A.f4("\u26a0\ufe0f","Avoid the #1 mistake",A.b(["Before judging any result, check the top-bar environment badge. If it says Development you are hitting localhost; if it says Production you are hitting the online anchor. Testing prod behaviour while on dev (or vice-versa) gives misleading results."],j)),new A.f4("\ud83d\udd10","9 \xb7 Login & sessions (web + mobile + manage)",A.b(["ONE login everywhere: your saved email + saved password + a random CODE shown on the DESKTOP. Web, mobile and the anchor Manage page all sign in the same way.",'The code is DIFFERENT and RANDOM for each target and each attempt \u2014 tap "Get code" in the app, then read the code from the desktop\'s blinking "Connecting with Anchor" badge (it shows which of web / mobile / manage needs to connect).',"The session lasts 7 DAYS, then it auto-logs-out and asks you to sign in again. No anonymous access: without a valid login the anchor returns 401 for web/mobile reads and command submits.","LOGOUT is a clear button in the top bar \u2014 visible in normal mode AND chat mode, on both web and mobile. Log out any time to end the session early.","Mobile Face ID is OPTIONAL: if the device supports it, it can unlock; if not, the email+password+code login always works (never blocked).","Only the DESKTOP can approve a login (it shows the code) \u2014 so only you, at your machine, can let a web/mobile client in."],j)),new A.f4("\ud83d\udcf2","10 \xb7 Install the app on a real iPhone (no App Store)",A.b(['1) Connect the iPhone by cable, unlock it, tap Trust. Open Xcode once so it "Prepares" the device (first time can take minutes) \u2014 then flutter can see it.',"2) Open odin_app/ios/Runner.xcworkspace (the WORKSPACE, not the .xcodeproj). Runner target \u2192 Signing & Capabilities \u2192 Automatically manage signing \u2192 Team \u2192 Add your Apple ID (free) and pick your Personal Team. Bundle id is a neutral personal one (com.mostafaadawy.mobileapp).","3) Install a RELEASE build (debug apps cannot launch from the home screen on iOS 14+): flutter run --release -d <iphone-id> --dart-define=ODIN_FORCE_ENV=production --dart-define=ODIN_ANCHOR=https://anchor.odinmarkets.com/odin-anchor","4) On the phone: Settings \u2192 General \u2192 VPN & Device Management \u2192 your Apple ID \u2192 Trust. Then open the app from the home screen.","Free Apple ID = the app runs for 7 days, then re-run step 3 to renew. It talks only to the online anchor, so it works over any internet from a separate device."],j))],t.L2)
